1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Why do 90% of AI agents fail in production?

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Nobody talks about the real reason, and it is not the model.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:15,000
It is the missing evaluation loop that catches broken tool calls early.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Teams ship an agent, watch it for a day, and assume that it works.

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Instead, write ten test prompts and run them on every single change.

6
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:33,000
That one habit cuts silent failures by more than half in my own projects.

7
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:38,000
So the lesson is simple. Test the agent the way you test code.

8
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:44,000
um so yeah and like basically we also had a call about the schedule

9
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:50,000
and um you know the weather was kind of nice that day anyway

10
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:54,000
How do you test an agent in under five minutes?

11
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Start with three prompts: one easy, one tricky and one that should be refused.

12
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:07,000
Run them after each change and compare the outputs side by side.

13
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:13,000
You will catch regressions in seconds instead of days.

14
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:19,000
Save the best outputs as your baseline and keep them in git.
